WEBVTT

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.840
That wasn't a dream... was it? 

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.950
Joey, what's the matter? 

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.590
I-It's nothing! 

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.540
Come on now, is something the matter? 

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:25.010
No, seriously! It's nothing, really! 

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:27.400
Can you leave me alone for a bit? 

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.280
<i>Please! Stop!</i>

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.110
Joey's acting strange... 

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:42.740
Don't be frightened. 

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:46.080
All that happened is some lighting struck our house and damaged it. 

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:25.530
Heroman... Go! 

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.870
W-What am I going to do? 

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:04.950
Even if you have an expression like this,

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:10.530
if you factor it into primes you can still solve for the least common multiple. 

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:14.310
All you need to do is think of it just like how you deal with numbers,

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:17.250
and take the prime factor with the highest exponent. 

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.500
Joey! 

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.970
Pay attention. 

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.140
Right! I'm sorry... 

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:26.340
For example: Like the previous expressions,

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.000
if you have an x and an x cubed...

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.230
Psy's got his part time job, huh? 

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.910
Give me V! 

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.390
Give me I! 

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:40.900
Give me C-T-O-R-Y! VICTORY! 

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.390
Joey! 

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:53.220
Lina! 

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:56.960
Don't worry, my brother and his gang aren't around. 

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:59.040
Anyway, did you hear? 

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:02.920
When we had that storm the other day, something <i>amazing</i> happened! 

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:09.190
I was caught up in an accident and me and my dad were trapped in our car. 

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:10.470
But then... 

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:13.640
I-I don't know a thing about that! 

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:16.050
I don't know anything! 

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:17.400
It had nothing to do with me! 

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.500
Is something the matter? 

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.270
Sorry, I have stuff to do. 

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:21.720
Gotta go! 

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:25.650
Joey's acting strange... 

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.360
Something the matter? 

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.090
Don't scare me like that... 

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:47.580
You're the one that's scaring <i>me</i>. 

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:49.920
What's with you lately? 

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:52.220
Are you hiding something from me? 

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:55.310
No... That's not it.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:58.730
Say that, hypothetically... 

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:03.200
If a hero appeared before you one day, Grandma,

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:08.170
and it turned out he'd do anything you told him to... 

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:09.480
What would you do? 

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:12.660
Do you have a fever or something? 

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:16.590
I told you, hypothetically... 

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.620
Well...

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:23.460
For the time being, how about trimming the grass for me?

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.680
So, that's the deal. 

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.680
What do you think, Psy? 

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.330
Hold it a sec. 

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:44.180
I don't get what you're saying. 

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:46.070
Neither do I. 

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:48.920
Can something like this even really happen? 

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:56.660
Uh, so basically this "Heroman" turned into a giant and saved Lina? 

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:01.520
But Heroman here holds amazing power... 

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:02.660
Yeah. 

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:06.220
What do you think I should do? 

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:12.150
Is it really okay for me to have a robot with such amazing power? 

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:15.560
Maybe I should hide it somewhere... 

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:18.040
Look here, Joey. 

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:21.180
What is Heroman to you? 

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:27.690
Welcome! 

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:32.820
You answer that question first, and then figure out what to do. 

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:36.700
Don't rely on other people's opinions. You have to make this decision yourself.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.200
Hey, Psy... 

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:43.680
What would you do if you were me? 

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:48.700
I'd jump in bed and go back to sleep. 

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:51.460
Then maybe I'd wake up from the dream. 

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:02.890
Heroman, what should I do? 

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:16.480
<i>Hello, hello, to my unseen friends and neighbors!</i>

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:22.230
<i>I am Prof. Matthew Denton, representing the third planet of the solar system.</i>

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:26.730
<i>We Earthlings wish to make contact with you!</i>

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:29.710
<i>Please, respond!</i>

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:34.460
<i>Hello, hello, to my unseen friends and neighbors!</i>

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:39.900
<i>I am Prof. Matthew Denton, representing the third planet of the solar system.</i>

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:49.440
Huh?

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.320
What's that? 

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:25.890
Whoa, it's aliens! 

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:27.540
What? Another TV shoot? 

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:29.590
Wait, isn't that my car?! 

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:57.670
It's a movie... Gotta be a movie shoot. 

00:10:57.670 --> 00:10:59.230
Hey, you people! 

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:03.140
If you want to film a movie, you need to get a permit first! 

00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:31.460
Hey, what's that? 

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:34.290
Seems like something's going on. 

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:37.370
What's all the fuss about? 

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:41.510
Let's go check it out! 

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.790
Hey, wait, Will! 

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:57.320
That's far enough! 

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.760
Throw down your weapons and surrender immediately! 

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:03.070
You're completely surrounded! 

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:04.490
I repeat! 

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:07.420
Throw down your weapons and surrender! 

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:12.910
If you do not comply with our warning, we're willing to use force! 

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:14.500
Throw down your weapons... 

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:27.510
Open fire! 

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.400
Holy... Is this some kind of a joke? 

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:41.600
Guns... have no effect! 

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:42.780
They're monsters! 

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:51.660
Lord Kogorr, reporting in. 

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:57.410
Their level of civilization is low, and their military and offensive capabilities are nothing to fear. 

00:12:57.410 --> 00:13:01.160
The composition of the atmosphere is also within our operational limits. 

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:02.570
I see... 

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:04.570
I'd like more information. 

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:09.680
Search out the source of the interplanetary communication signal, and bring me the one responsible for it.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:13.110
I wish to use him as a sample... 

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:14.540
Understood. 

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:16.750
We have already locked on to the signal. 

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:19.190
Do not fail me. 

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:28.170
Are you sure we're not dreaming? 

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:30.750
Will, we've got to run away, too! 

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:32.160
Run away? 

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:33.400
Yeah! 

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:35.410
If we don't hurry up, we'll get caught up in it ourselves! 

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:41.380
<i>We've received information that the explosion at the intersection in Center City</i>

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:44.060
<i>was due to an attack by some unknown group. </i>

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:45.700
What's going on? 

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:46.680
<i>According to eye-witnesses,</i>

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:49.800
<i>the ones responsible were three... aliens?! </i>

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:50.590
Aliens? 

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:54.930
I contacted intelligent extraterrestrial life forms!

00:13:55.670 --> 00:13:56.810
It couldn't be... 

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:59.980
Anyway, this sounds bad. Joey... 

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:02.610
Hey, Joey! Where are you going? 

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:17.860
Prof. Denton! 

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:19.080
What's up? 

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.870
Why're you giving me that look? 

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:23.760
Well, seems like something's going on outside, but... 

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:25.120
It's bad! 

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:28.480
I know this sounds crazy, but they're already here!

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:52.570
Is it you? 

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:54.330
It spoke! 

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:57.410
We are the Skrugg.  

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:01.540
Are you the one broadcasting the interplanetary signal? 

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:04.250
Yes! That would be me! 

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:09.260
So you picked up my signal and came here, right? 

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:10.630
That is correct. 

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:15.760
This is all because of that signal which you are broadcasting.

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:19.350
I bid you welcome! As the representative for humanity!

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:22.560
That will not be necessary. 

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:25.020
Because, we... 

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:33.280
Because we are beings that will destroy this planet. 

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:38.790
Destroy... this planet? 

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:43.760
We will bring you with us as the representative for humanity. 

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:50.880
In order to extract various information from your memory area. 

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:52.650
What do you... 

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:55.540
Let us also take the one with you. 

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:58.260
The more samples, the better. 

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:00.340
Me, too? 

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:07.060
Looks like we've got ourselves another sample. 

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.080
Professor! 

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:16.910
This is my responsibility! 

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:20.200
You expect to resist us with that? 

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:28.750
Go, run! 

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:35.090
Don't rely on other people's opinions. You have to make this decision yourself.

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:41.470
What's the matter? Get out of here, Joey! 

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:43.550
No, I'm not leaving! 

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:49.210
I might... No... 

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:51.420
<i>He</i> might be able to do something! 

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:18.470
Heroman...

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:20.890
Engage! 

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:53.480
What?! 

00:17:59.710 --> 00:18:01.060
That's... 

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:03.170
Are you okay?

00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:04.170
Sure...

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:06.730
But... 

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:09.730
That robot... 

00:18:13.310 --> 00:18:14.780
Was it... 

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:24.220
You want some? 

00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:39.680
Lina! 

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:45.930
Lina! 

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:06.510
Joey... 

00:19:09.570 --> 00:19:11.230
Heroman! 

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:12.330
Joey? 

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:13.600
Stay here. 

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:17.580
I've got this power inside me, too! 

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:29.310
Let's do this, Heroman. 

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:40.010
Lina, are you okay? 

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:42.420
Joey is... Joey is... 

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:45.450
Whoa... 

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:06.300
I can't believe this! 

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:08.930
Heroman! 

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:20.440
Stay back! 

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:21.740
Stay back! 

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:41.170
Heroman...

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:44.410
Finish! 

00:21:05.770 --> 00:21:07.180
Joey! 

00:21:11.030 --> 00:21:12.610
You did it, Joey! 

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:13.380
Yeah! 

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:16.360
Heroman is our hero! 

00:21:16.360 --> 00:21:17.500
Nope... 

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:20.750
That's not right, Joey. 

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:23.420
You're <i>both</i> heroes! 

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:25.250
Both of us? 

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:36.080
What in the world... 

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:39.270
Joey... 

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:24.090
<b>"Can you hear this voice?"</b>

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:31.560
<b>I've been calling that, always, from deep within my heart.</b>

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:45.460
<b>Would you, all alone, let another lonely one be next to you?</b>

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:51.010
<b>Because together it's not lonely, it's twoly.</b>

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:56.140
<b>See, you're not alone any longer.</b>

00:22:57.280 --> 00:22:59.990
<b>Just because there's no one next to me</b>

00:22:59.990 --> 00:23:02.540
<b>doesn't mean that I'm lonely!</b>

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:07.740
<b>For someone to notice this pain</b>

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:13.270
<b>that heart must have surely cried.</b>

00:23:13.270 --> 00:23:16.650
<b>Right now, we'll crush to bits</b>

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:20.350
<b>the fortress of our limitless sadness!</b>

00:23:20.350 --> 00:23:24.050
<b>I'll take you with me!</b>

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:27.730
<b>Got it? I'm running through at full power.</b>

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:31.470
<b>To where you're waiting, left behind</b>

00:23:31.470 --> 00:23:34.640
<b>in the place of tears...</b>

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:39.770
<b>I believe in you, with burning passion!</b>

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:43.560
<b>Come to me!</b>

00:23:50.770 --> 00:23:52.710
On the next Heroman: 

00:23:52.710 --> 00:23:54.590
Oh, no, Prof. Denton! 

00:23:54.590 --> 00:23:56.200
A giant Skrugg saucer is here! 

00:23:56.500 --> 00:23:59.990
It seemed liked the invaders were driven away thanks to Heroman's actions,

00:23:59.990 --> 00:24:03.330
but it was just a prelude to the coming battle.

00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:06.040
Under the command of their leader, Kogorr,

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:11.560
the Skrugg have begun their Earth invasion, and humanity's forces are at their wit's end.

00:24:12.340 --> 00:24:15.970
Next time, Heroman Episode #3: Invasion!

00:24:15.970 --> 00:24:19.000
Heroman... Attack!
